<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Thy name we love, Lord Jesus;</l><l>It tells God’s love unbounded</l><l>To ruined man, ere time began,</l><l>Or heav’n and earth were founded:</l><l>Thine is a love eternal,</l><l>That found in us its pleasure,</l><l>That brought Thee low to bear our woe</l><l>And make us Thine own treasure.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Thy name we love, Lord Jesus;</l><l>It tells Thy birth so lowly,</l><l>Thy patience, grace, and gentleness,</l><l>Thy lonely path, so holy;</l><l>Thou wast the “Man of Sorrows“;</l><l>Our grief, too, Thou didst bear it;</l><l>Our bitter cup Thou drankest up;</l><l>The thorny crown, didst wear it.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Thy name we love, Lord Jesus;</l><l>God’s Lamb—Thou wast ordained,</l><l>To bear our sins (Thyself all clean)</l><l>And hast our guilt sustained.</l><l>We see Thee crowned in glory,</l><l>Above the heavens now seated,</l><l>The vict’ry won, Thy work well done,</l><l>Our righteousness completed.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
